# distributed-systems-lab

A hands-on lab for exploring core **Software Engineering roles and frameworks** — backend, AI/ML engineering, DevOps, and data engineering — through small, simple, runnable examples.

The goal isn't theory. Each folder is a minimal, working mock project you can spin up in minutes, see real results (traces, logs, metrics), and understand *why* the concept matters — before applying it to real systems.

## What's in here

| Area | Frameworks/Tools | What you'll find |
|---|---|---|
| **Messaging** | RabbitMQ, Celery | Publisher/consumer patterns, async task queues |
| **Observability** | OpenTelemetry, Jaeger, Prometheus, Grafana | Instrumentation, distributed tracing, metrics |
| **Caching** | Redis | Cache-aside, write-back patterns |
| **Mock projects** | FastAPI + all of the above combined | End-to-end pipelines simulating real-world scenarios (e.g. an email processing pipeline, a bakery process) |

## Structure

```
distributed-systems-lab/
├── messaging/       # RabbitMQ, Celery examples
├── observability/   # OpenTelemetry, Jaeger, Prometheus experiments
├── caching/         # Redis patterns
└── mock-projects/   # Combined end-to-end examples (email pipeline, bakery, etc.)
```

## Philosophy

- **Simple over complete.** Every example is intentionally minimal — just enough code to see the concept work.
- **Runnable in minutes.** Docker Compose where needed, plain scripts where not.
- **See it, don't just read it.** Every example produces something visible — a trace in Jaeger, a log line, a dashboard — not just passing tests.
- **Build up gradually.** Start with one moving part (a single traced function), then combine (queue + tracing + caching) once each piece is understood on its own.

## Getting started

Each subfolder has its own short README with:
1. What the example demonstrates
2. The code, in full
3. The exact commands to run it
4. What to expect when you look at the results

Start with `observability/` if you're new to tracing — it's the foundation most other examples build on.

## Requirements

- Docker & Docker Compose
- [uv](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv) for Python dependency management
- A running `shared_net` Docker network (`docker network create shared_net`)

## Roadmap

More examples will be added over time covering additional SWE, AI Engineering, DevOps, and Data Engineering topics as they come up in study/interview prep.